          "type": "content",
          "heading": "Deep study: Backup and versioning",
          "text": "A spreadsheet may contain many hours of work and important records. Saving a backup before major structural changes can protect against mistakes. Version names should be meaningful, such as including a date or revision number. The objective is to make it possible to identify the most recent trustworthy copy rather than creating many confusing “final” versions."
